'''Skorr'''<ref name="Whills Strike Back">{{StoryCite|story=The Whills Strike Back|book=From a Certain Point of View: The Empire Strikes Back}}</ref> was a [[bounty hunter]] who operated sometime prior to the [[Battle of Hoth]] and engaged a group of [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance personnel]] on [[Ord Mantell]]. The group included the [[Alderaanian]] [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] and the [[freighter]] [[captain]] [[Han Solo]]. Later, as Solo prepared to abandon the Alliance on [[Hoth]], he cited the encounter with Skorr as a reason for his departure to Organa.<ref name="TESB" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Skorr was first mentioned in the [[1980]] film [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''The Empire Strikes Back'']], written by [[Leigh Brackett]] and [[Lawrence Kasdan]].<ref name="TESB" /> In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, several different accounts were given for the encounter between Solo and the hunter. The now obsolete [[StarWars.com]] [[Databank (original)|Databank]] identified the hunter as [[Skorr/Legends|Skorr]],<ref name="DB">{{DB|location|ordmantell|Ord Mantell}}</ref> a character first introduced in the [[1981]] comic strip ''[[The Bounty Hunter of Ord Mantell]]'', written by [[Archie Goodwin]] and illustrated by [[Al Williamson]].<ref name="BHoOM">"[[The Bounty Hunter of Ord Mantell]]"</ref> The bounty hunter was eventually identified in the short story "[[The Whills Strike Back]]," written by [[Tom Angleberger]] and published in [[2020]] as part of the anthology book ''[[From a Certain Point of View: The Empire Strikes Back]].''<ref name="Whills Strike Back" />

In the ''[[Star Wars Forces of Destiny]]'' episode [[Bounty Hunted]], a character resembling Skorr's Legends appearance appears as a background character.<ref name="Bounty Hunted">{{FOD|Bounty Hunted}}</ref>

